Fix the vendored bash-preexec include path for the crates.io tarball

Upstream keeps bash-preexec at <repo-root>/vendor/bash-preexec/, i.e. three
levels above crates/atuin/src/. The published .crate is flattened to
atuin-<version>/src/, so the relative path escapes the extracted tree and
the include_str! fails. We install the script at <crate-root>/bash-preexec/
in %prep instead (not vendor/, which belongs to cargo-vendor) and point the
macro at it.

Not suitable for upstream: upstream should relocate the script under
crates/atuin/ or emit it into OUT_DIR from a build script so that builds
from crates.io work at all.

--- a/src/shell.rs
+++ b/src/shell.rs
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 pub const BASH: Bash<'_> = Bash {
     include_guard: include_shell!("atuin.bash.d/include-guard.bash"),
     main: include_shell!("atuin.bash"),
-    preexec: include_trimmed!("../../../vendor/bash-preexec/bash-preexec.sh"),
+    preexec: include_trimmed!("../bash-preexec/bash-preexec.sh"),
 };
 
 pub const FISH: &str = include_shell!("atuin.fish");
